{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Sets a function to be called at regular intervals, with the default","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"priority, [const"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/priorityDefault","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"].","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/timeoutAdd(interval:function:data:)"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/glib\/timeoutadd(interval:function:data:)"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"timeoutAdd","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"interval","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"function"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@GSourceFunc","text":"GSourceFunc","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"text":"data","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"gpointer","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@gpointer"},{"text":"? = nil) -> ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The given "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"function"},{"text":" is called repeatedly until it returns","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"[const","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/sourceRemove","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"], at which point the timeout is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"automatically destroyed and the function will not be called again. The first"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"call to the function will be at the end of the first ","type":"text"},{"code":"interval","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Note that timeout functions may be delayed, due to the processing of other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"event sources. Thus they should not be relied on for precise timing.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"After each call to the timeout function, the time of the next"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"timeout is recalculated based on the current time and the given interval","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"(it does not try to ‘catch up’ time lost in delays)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"identifier":"main-loop.html#memory-management-of-sources","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for details"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"on how to handle the return value and memory management of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"data"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If you want to have a timer in the ‘seconds’ range and do not care","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"about the exact time of the first call of the timer, use the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"[func"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.timeout_add_seconds"},{"type":"text","text":"] function; this function allows for more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"optimizations and more efficient system power usage."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This internally creates a main loop source using","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"[func"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.timeout_source_new"},{"type":"text","text":"] and attaches it to the global"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"[struct","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MainContext","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"] using [method"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.Source.attach"},{"text":"], so the callback","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"will be invoked in whichever thread is running that main context. You can do"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"these steps manually if you need greater control or to use a custom main","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It is safe to call this function from any thread.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The interval given is in terms of monotonic time, not wall clock","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"time. See [func"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.get_monotonic_time"},{"text":"].","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib"]]},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"func","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"timeoutAdd","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"interval","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"function"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@GSourceFunc","text":"GSourceFunc","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"data"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@gpointer","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"gpointer"},{"text":"?) -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"GLib"}],"roleHeading":"Function","externalID":"s:4